e scale is 1.279", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["odds ratio"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 100, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[155, 156]], "assertion": "each 0.1-unit increase in skin tone is associated with a 2.5% increase in odds of red card, not statistically significant once multiple comparisons are considered", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["continuous skin tone effect"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 101, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[157, 157]], "note": "extended model subheading"}, {"id": 102, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[158, 158]], "assertion": "yellow cards received was included as a covariate in an extended model as a potential mediator", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["yellow cards"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 103, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[159, 159]], "assertion": "in the extended model, dark skin OR is 1.170 (95% CI 0.974-1.406)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["odds ratio"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 104, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[160, 161]], "assertion": "the extended-model result is similar to the primary analysis, though yellow cards may lie on the causal pathway", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["extended model result"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 105, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[162, 163]], "note": "missing data subheading and intro"}, {"id": 106, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[164, 164]], "assertion": "red card rate is 1.26% for players with ratings vs 1.14% for those without, described as similar", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["missing data comparison"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 107, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[165, 166]], "assertion": "games per dyad is 2.99 with ratings vs 2.50 without, associated with fewer games but not substantially different red card rates", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["missing data comparison"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 108, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[167, 168]], "assertion": "missing data appears related to photo availability rather than outcomes, reducing concern about selection bias", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["missing data mechanism"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 109, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[169, 170]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 110, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[171, 172]], "note": "section 7 heading"}, {"id": 111, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[173, 173]], "note": "statistical power subheading"}, {"id": 112, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[174, 174]], "assertion": "the study may be underpowered to detect the observed effect size", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["statistical power"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 113, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[175, 175]], "assertion": "minimum detectable effect at 80% power, α=0.05 is 0.258 percentage points", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["minimum detectable effect"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 114, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[176, 176]], "assertion": "observed effect is 0.211 percentage points", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["observed effect"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 115, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[177, 178]], "assertion": "observed effect is 82% of the minimum detectable effect", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["power ratio"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 116, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[179, 180]], "assertion": "the observed effect being below the MDE explains why the CI includes zero, and a larger sample would be needed to establish an effect", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["statistical power"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 117, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[181, 181]], "note": "measurement issues subheading"}, {"id": 118, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[182, 183]], "note": "caveat that photo-based skin tone rating may not capture what referees perceive"}, {"id": 119, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[184, 185]], "note": "caveat that dichotomizing skin tone loses information and reduces power"}, {"id": 120, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[186, 187]], "note": "caveat that collapsing red card counts to binary loses granularity"}, {"id": 121, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[188, 188]], "note": "confounding subheading"}, {"id": 122, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[189, 195]], "note": "caveat listing possible unmeasured confounders not in the dataset"}, {"id": 123, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[196, 197]], "note": "caveat that referee-level confounding beyond country bias is not fully addressed"}, {"id": 124, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[198, 199]], "note": "caveat about possible time-varying confounding over career span"}, {"id": 125, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[200, 200]], "note": "selection bias subheading"}, {"id": 126, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[201, 202]], "note": "caveat about possible selection bias from missing photos"}, {"id": 127, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[203, 204]], "note": "caveat about generalizability beyond top European leagues"}, {"id": 128, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[205, 206]], "note": "caveat about possible survival bias"}, {"id": 129, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[207, 207]], "note": "causal interpretation subheading"}, {"id": 130, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[208, 212]], "note": "caveat that the study is observational and cannot establish causation"}, {"id": 131, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[213, 213]], "note": "multiple comparisons subheading"}, {"id": 132, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[214, 215]], "note": "caveat about multiple testing concerns given p=0.107"}, {"id": 133, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[216, 217]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 134, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[218, 219]], "note": "section 8 heading"}, {"id": 135, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[220, 220]], "note": "assumptions met subheading"}, {"id": 136, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[221, 221]], "assertion": "random sampling within the study frame was assumed met, with all players in top leagues included", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["random sampling"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 137, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[222, 222]], "assertion": "sample size was adequate, with a dataset of over 100,000 dyads", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sample size"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 138, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[223, 223]], "assertion": "measurement reliability was high, with inter-rater agreement r=0.92 on skin tone", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["inter-rater reliability"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 139, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[224, 224]], "assertion": "logistic regression was deemed the appropriate specification for the binary outcome", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["model specification"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 140, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[225, 226]], "assertion": "clustering was addressed via cluster-robust SEs accounting for player-level correlation", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["clustering"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 141, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[227, 227]], "note": "assumptions with limitations subheading"}, {"id": 142, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[228, 228]], "note": "caveat that unmeasured confounding is still possible"}, {"id": 143, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[229, 229]], "note": "caveat that missingness may not be completely random"}, {"id": 144, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[230, 230]], "note": "caveat that players with longer careers are over-represented"}, {"id": 145, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[231, 232]], "note": "caveat that effect homogeneity was not explored"}, {"id": 146, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[233, 234]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 147, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[235, 236]], "note": "section 9 heading"}, {"id": 148, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[237, 237]], "note": "primary finding subheading"}, {"id": 149, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[238, 239]], "assertion": "after adjustment, dark-skinned players had a 0.211 pp (CI -0.045 to 0.482) higher probability of a red card, not statistically significant (p=0.107)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["adjusted risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 150, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[240, 240]], "note": "effect size context subheading"}, {"id": 151, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[241, 241]], "assertion": "the absolute effect is described as small (0.21 pp)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect size"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 152, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[242, 242]], "assertion": "in relative terms the effect represents a 17% increase over the 1.22% baseline risk", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["relative effect size"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 153, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[243, 244]], "assertion": "practically, the effect translates to about 2 additional red cards per 1,000 dyads for dark-skinned players", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["practical significance"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 154, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[245, 245]], "note": "statistical significance subheading"}, {"id": 155, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[246, 246]], "assertion": "the hypothesis is not supported at α=0.05", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["hypothesis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 156, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[247, 247]], "assertion": "the 95% CI includes zero", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["confidence interval"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 157, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[248, 248]], "assertion": "the p-value (0.107) exceeds 0.05", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["p-value"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 158, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[249, 250]], "assertion": "the point estimate is smaller than the minimum detectable effect for adequate power", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["minimum detectable effect"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 159, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[251, 251]], "note": "interpretation subheading"}, {"id": 160, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[252, 253]], "note": "restates that evidence is inconclusive and introduces three possible interpretations"}, {"id": 161, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[254, 254]], "assertion": "one possible interpretation is a true null effect, with no systematic bias by skin tone", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["interpretation: true null"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 162, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[255, 255]], "assertion": "another possible interpretation is a small true effect (~0.2pp) that the study is underpowered to detect significantly", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["interpretation: underpowered small effect"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 163, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[256, 257]], "assertion": "another possible interpretation is that the observed association reflects unmeasured confounding rather than bias", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["interpretation: confounded association"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 164, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[258, 259]], "assertion": "the data cannot distinguish among these interpretations; estimates are consistent with a small positive association but insufficient to reject the null", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["overall interpretation"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 165, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[260, 260]], "note": "recommendation subheading"}, {"id": 166, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[261, 262]], "assertion": "a larger study or meta-analysis, or an experimental/quasi-experimental design, would have been preferred to definitively test the effect", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["future study design"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 167, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[263, 264]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 168, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[265, 266]], "note": "section 10 heading"}, {"id": 169, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[267, 267]], "assertion": "analyses are fully reproducible using the code in final_analysis.py", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["reproducibility"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 170, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[268, 268]], "assertion": "used the packages pandas, numpy, statsmodels, scipy, and scikit-learn", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["software packages"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 171, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[269, 269]], "assertion": "used a fixed random seed (42) for bootstrap resampling", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["random seed"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 172, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[270, 270]], "assertion": "used a publicly described data source and codebook", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["data source"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 173, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[271, 272]], "assertion": "provided transparent reporting of all analytical decisions", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["reporting"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 174, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[273, 274]], "assertion": "data source is soccer player-referee dyads from European leagues (2012-2013) from a sports statistics company, with 146,028 dyads, 2,053 players, and 3,147 referees across England, Germany, France, and Spain", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["data source"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 175, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[275, 276]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 176, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[277, 278]], "note": "completion date and software version line"}, {"id": 177, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[279, 280]], "note": "blank line and end marker"}]}}